          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "This is a detailed description of a bug fix needed for LVGL's GIF handling. Let me understand what needs to be done:\n\n1. When a GIF is assigned to an LVGL GIF object, the image descriptor needs to be properly populated with:\n   - Magic number\n   - Flags\n   - Color format (ARGB8888)\n   - Width, height\n   - Stride (width * 4 bytes)\n   - Total data size\n   - Canvas pointer as data pointer\n\n2. Previously opened GIFs need to be cleanly closed and cache entries dropped before loading new sources\n\n3. The object structure should hold an LVGL image descriptor instead of a generic draw buffer\n\n4. After the fix, setting a GIF source should result in a correctly sized, modifiable image that animates properly\n\nLet me search for the relevant GIF-related code in the LVGL codebase to understand the current implementation and what needs to be fixed.\n",
